# Board records for boardscore.cpp. These four boards are FICTIONAL examples that show the
# format; replace them with records you research yourself (one field per line, values as in
# the chapter's table). A field you could not find out: leave it out (it scores nothing).
board Board P (fictional)
trm full
errata yes
boot_chain open
dram_init blob
mainline_linux yes
mainline_uboot yes
recovery usb
uart yes
uart_note 3-pin header next to the GPIO connector; signal level in the schematic

board Board Q (fictional)
trm partial
errata no
boot_chain open
dram_init open
mainline_linux partial
mainline_uboot yes
recovery sd
uart yes
uart_note test pads on the back of the board

board Board R (fictional)
trm full
errata yes
boot_chain locked
mainline_linux yes
recovery usb
uart yes

board Board S (fictional)
boot_chain payload
mainline_linux partial
recovery sd
uart no
